asonNumber\":1,\"seasonName\":\"Miniseries\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/33EO8kdefS4Z5SgCJDhLt39HHLE.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2025-03-03\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Chapter I: Founding Fathers\",\"overview\":\"Led by Bob Cousy and Bill Russell, the Celtics become an NBA dynasty, but racial tensions in Boston and beyond augur a turbulent era ahead.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yLfXQL8tMxKLt3AdxmSrJM8l2fR.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-03-03\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Chapter II: No Final Victories\",\"overview\":\"Amid backlash for his commitment to civil rights, Bill Russell makes history as the first Black head coach in professional sports.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/iSRSN9MubjWZUkoqIeBZNoFguk7.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-03-10\",\"runtime\":59},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Chapter III: All Swept Up\",\"overview\":\"The Celtics win a pair of titles in the '70s amid racial unrest, and near the end of the decade, they draft Indiana State star Larry Bird.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/48aUSlh621b0uJEAiL6gXQBLubj.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-03-17\",\"runtime\":59},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Chapter IV: Great Hope. Period.\",\"overview\":\"Larry Bird elevates the Celtics and struggling NBA to new heights, but internal discord threatens to derail another potential dynasty.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/kP9M22FxyNdVEtsFhbFOm7IKDFg.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-03-24\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Chapter V: F**k the Celtics\",\"overview\":\"Larry Bird's epic rivalry with Magic Johnson captivates the sports world. Then, in 1986, an unthinkable tragedy changes everything.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/tD26uhYe3aXdAnc30geceJTqJxl.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-03-31\",\"runtime\":59},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Chapter VI: Untenable Toll\",\"overview\":\"The tragic death of Len Bias casts a shadow over the Celtics. In 1992, Larry Bird's retirement closes a chapter for the team and the NBA.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/c7SIFLOl4Zd46WUOpjFGLrMqoWv.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-04-07\",\"runtime\":59},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Chapter VII: Not Again\",\"overview\":\"After Reggie Lewis' sudden death leaves the city heartbroken, the Celtics spiral into steep decline following the arrival of Rick Pitino.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/3zJaRrMn217JmaqJQ8z4VWVPFsV.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-04-14\",\"runtime\":59},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Chapter VIII: Ubuntu\",\"overview\":\"After another downturn, new GM and former Celtic Danny Ainge acquires Kevin Garnett and Ray Allen to form a \\\"Big Three\\\" with Paul Pierce.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/A8iiELl4BupvS44FUy39x7aB5tW.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-04-21\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Chapter IX: We're the Celtics\",\"overview\":\"After the 2008 title, injuries, and internal conflict take a toll. Led by a new crop of stars, the team wins an 18th championship in 2024.​\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/8qzgd0mxmRbqKkj2fmRA3hStF25.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2025-04-28\",\"runtime\":60}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2025-03-03\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}